@baseUrl = http://localhost:5000

### login as asset manager first (see auth-req.http, use assets@sdp.test)

### list assets
GET {{baseUrl}}/asset-api/assets

### warranty-expiring report (default 30 days)
GET {{baseUrl}}/asset-api/assets/warranty-expiring

### create an asset
POST {{baseUrl}}/asset-api/assets
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "HP EliteBook 840",
  "type": "HARDWARE",
  "assetClass": "Laptop",
  "serialNumber": "HP840-0099",
  "purchaseCost": 82000,
  "warrantyExpiry": "2027-01-01"
}

### full lifecycle walk (replace PASTE_ASSET_ID with the publicId, e.g. AST-2026-00005)

### PROCURED -> IN_STOCK
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/asset-api/assets/PASTE_ASSET_ID/activate
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "version": 1
}

### IN_STOCK -> ASSIGNED (assignedTo required)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/asset-api/assets/PASTE_ASSET_ID/assign
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "assignedTo": "PASTE_USER_ID",
  "version": 1
}

### ASSIGNED -> IN_STOCK (returned)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/asset-api/assets/PASTE_ASSET_ID/return
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "version": 1
}

### IN_STOCK/ASSIGNED -> IN_REPAIR (also works logged in as a technician)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/asset-api/assets/PASTE_ASSET_ID/repair
Content-Type: application/json

{ "note": "screen flickering", "version": 1 }

### IN_REPAIR -> ASSIGNED (only if it still has an assignedTo on record)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/asset-api/assets/PASTE_ASSET_ID/reinstate
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "version": 1
}

### IN_REPAIR -> IN_STOCK (clears assignedTo)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/asset-api/assets/PASTE_ASSET_ID/restock
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "version": 1
}

### terminal: -> RETIRED
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/asset-api/assets/PASTE_ASSET_ID/retire
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "version": 1
}

### try ASSIGNED -> RETIRED directly (should 400 -- not in the transition table)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/asset-api/assets/PASTE_ASSET_ID/retire
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "version": 1
}

### replace an assigned/in-repair asset with one that's IN_STOCK
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/asset-api/assets/PASTE_OLD_ASSET_ID/replace
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "newAssetId": "PASTE_NEW_IN_STOCK_ASSET_ID",
  "note": "old unit had a failing battery",
  "version": 1
}

### add a maintenance entry
POST {{baseUrl}}/asset-api/assets/PASTE_ASSET_ID/maintenance
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "type": "Repair",
  "cost": 1500,
  "note": "replaced keyboard"
}

### lifecycle history
GET {{baseUrl}}/asset-api/assets/PASTE_ASSET_ID/history

### tickets referencing this asset
GET {{baseUrl}}/asset-api/assets/PASTE_ASSET_ID/tickets

### my assets (login as any user with assigned assets, e.g. employee@sdp.test)
GET {{baseUrl}}/asset-api/my-assets

### link an asset to a ticket (employee can only pick their own assigned asset)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/ticket-api/tickets/PASTE_TICKET_ID/related-asset
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "assetId": "PASTE_MY_ASSET_ID"
}

### --- SECURE-CORE: negative cases ---
### every transition needs the ticket's/asset's current "version" (read it from GET).

### no version -> 400 (version is required)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/asset-api/assets/PASTE_ASSET_ID/activate
Content-Type: application/json

{}

### stale version -> 409 (someone else changed it; refetch and retry)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/asset-api/assets/PASTE_ASSET_ID/activate
Content-Type: application/json

{ "version": 999 }

### version must be an integer -> 400
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/asset-api/assets/PASTE_ASSET_ID/activate
Content-Type: application/json

{ "version": "1" }

### /replace also needs version -> 400 without it
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/asset-api/assets/PASTE_OLD_ASSET_ID/replace
Content-Type: application/json

{ "newAssetId": "PASTE_NEW_IN_STOCK_ASSET_ID" }

### paging: limit is clamped to 1-50 and page to >= 1 (response has items, total, page, totalPages)
GET {{baseUrl}}/asset-api/assets?limit=0&page=-3

### array/object filters are ignored, not turned into a Mongo operator
GET {{baseUrl}}/asset-api/assets?status[$ne]=RETIRED&type[]=HARDWARE
